**The chain of truth.** Neo (Figma) is the design system. The ProGet packages are Neo built into shippable code. Storybook is those packages rendered and documented. The two example projects are Neo applied to real products. They should all agree; where they don't, the ruling order is:

`shipped package > Storybook > Neo Figma > example projects > existing standard doc`

Rationale: an agent's output is judged by what renders, so the code that ships wins. Neo outranks the example projects because the projects are consumers, not sources — a choice made in one project is a product decision until Neo or the package backs it up. Override this order here if it is wrong: `<<< >>>`

**The deliverable is exactly one file: `WORK_DIR/DESIGN-STANDARD.md`.** Everything else — findings, evidence, screenshots — is working material that lives alongside it and is not the deliverable. Generated specimen images are referenced from the standard and live in `WORK_DIR/assets/`.

