## 6. DEFINITION OF DONE

- [ ] Every phase file exists in `WORK_DIR/findings/`.
- [ ] Canonical tokens resolve with no nulls, no placeholders, provenance on every leaf.
- [ ] Zero uses of "appropriate", "consistent", "as needed", "modern" or "clean" as rules in the standard.
- [ ] Every SA-6 conflict appears either as a ruling in the standard or in `UNRESOLVED.md`.
- [ ] SA-10 built three screens from the setup block alone and, on its second run, was forced into no guesses on core foundations.
- [ ] The standard is one file, and its agent-brief section is self-sufficient for a routine screen.
- [ ] Drift report delivered separately to the design team, not buried in the standard.

## 7. GUARDRAILS

- Do not improve the design system while documenting it. Improvements go in the gap list.
- Do not let anti-AI research override house style. Ours wins; log the tension.
- Do not summarise a source you could not access. Say you could not access it.
- Do not compress a sub-agent's findings before writing them to disk. Compression happens once, in SA-9.
- In Figma you are read-only, and you never attempt a login yourself.
